 "score": "5", "director": "5"}, {"_id": 1779852382039.174, "label": "Packaging Design: Redesign a Product and  Modern Art & Ideas for a Brand from A to Z", "score": "5", "director": "5"}], "awards": [{"_id": 1779794344880.128, "date": "30/03/2026", "level": "National", "score": 10, "title": "Indian Art Contest", "agency": "MSME Ministry of Micro, Small & Medium Enterprises", "director": "10", "award_date": "30/03/2026"}], "society": [{"_id": 1779794344880.5278, "label": "Face Painting Activity, Sewa Parv 2025 ”Viksit bharat ke rang kala ke sang” & Tree Plantation", "score": "5", "details": "The School of Applied Arts & Crafts is organising a Face Painting Competition – 2025 under the banner of “Viksit Bharat Ke Rang, Kala Ke Sang.” The competition aims to provide a creative platform where participants can express their imagination, artistic skills, and innovative ideas through face painting. With exciting themes such as Fantasy & Magic, Social Issues, and Festivals, the event encourages participants to explore diverse subjects—ranging from mythical and imaginative visuals to socially relevant messages and cultural celebrations. This event not only promotes artistic expression but also fosters creativity, confidence, and a spirit of community within the institute. It promises to be a colorful and engaging celebration of art and ideas. Summary of Event:  Seva Parv 2025: Colours of a developed India with art The Ministry of Culture, Government of India is celebrating Seva Parv 2025 as a nationwide celebration of service, creativity and cultural pride from 17 September to 2 October 2025. Inspired by Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi's vision of a developed India by 2047, Seva Parv aims to bring together communities, institutions and individuals in a collective movement of service, creativity and cultural pride. As part of the ongoing Seva Parv 2025,( Information by https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleaseIframePage.aspx?PRID=2173828) & On the occasion of Earth Day, the School of Applied Arts and Crafts at D Y Patil International University organized a tree plantation activity on campus to promote environmental awareness and sustainability. As part of this initiative, one team of students actively participated in planting a rubber tree within the university premises. The activity aimed to encourage ecological responsibility, connect students with nature, and highlight the importance of green practices in everyday life. It also reinforced the value of environmental conservation through hands-on experience, making students more conscious of their role in protecting and nurturing the ecosystem for a sustainable future.", "activity": "Face Painting Activity, Sewa Parv 2025 ”Viksit bharat ke rang kala ke sang” & Tree Plantation", "director": "5"}, {"_id": 1779854252700.2124, "label": "EARTH DAY POSTER & Reel MAKING COMPETITION 2026", "score": "5", "details": "Coordinated the university-level Earth Day Awareness Poster Making Competition under the Bharat Environment Program – A Bharat Sustainability Campus Mission 2026. Managed student participation, registrations, communication, and overall event execution while promoting sustainability and environmental awareness through creative poster designs.", "activity": "EARTH DAY POSTER & Reel MAKING COMPETITION 2026", "director": "5"}], "uniActs": [{"_id": 1779794344880.5493, "score": 10, "nature": "social welfare - Viksit Bharat Abhiyan", "activity": "Coordinator of Face Painting Activity", "director": "10"}, {"_id": 1779855692308.674, "score": 10, "nature": "Social Welfare- Bharat Enviornment Programme 2026", "activity": "EARTH DAY POSTER MAKING COMPETITION 2026", "director": "10"}, {"_id": 1779874233731.2593, "score": 0, "nature": "Academic year Activity", "activity": "NAAC Criteria 5.1.2 Univesity level Coordinator", "director": "10"}, {"_id": 1779874288935.1028, "score": 0, "nature": "Short term based- Cutural Program", "activity": "Indust Fiesta Ramp Walk Coordinator", "director": "10"}, {"_i