cb237ca0-15e9-4a79-b7be-0cfa49c9afbd	sandesh.solepatil@dypiu.ac.in	2025-2026	ganesh.jadhav@dypiu.ac.in	hod	182.6333333333333257542108185589313507080078125	221	403.6333333333333257542108185589313507080078125	Dr. Solepatil is working as Program Coordinator and  admission Coordinator at department level. Also working as BoS Meeting Coordinator and Syllabus framing. Dr. Solepatil's contributions to the department are good. I strongly suggest focusing your efforts on securing external research funding.	{"acr": [{"hod": "4", "label": "Self-motivation and Proactiveness"}, {"hod": "4", "label": "Punctuality"}, {"hod": "5", "label": "Target based work"}, {"hod": "4", "label": "Effectiveness"}, {"hod": "4", "label": "Obedience"}], "ict": [{"hod": "5", "desc": "An innovative teaching-learning pedagogy was developed using customized 3D printed working models for subjects related to Kinematics of Mechanisms and Machine Elements. The pedagogy integrates physical visualization, motion analysis, and experiential learning to improve conceptual understanding of complex mechanical systems. Different mechanism models such as four-bar linkages, slider-crank mechanisms, Geneva mechanisms, cams and followers, and compliant mechanisms were designed and fabricated using additive manufacturing techniques.", "quad": "III", "type": "3D Printed Interactive Teaching Models, Experiential Learning Module, OBE-Based Activity, Project-Based Learning", "score": "5", "title": "Pedagogical Innovation Using 3D Printed Models for Teaching Kinematics of Mechanisms and Machine Elements", "director": "", "quadrant": "III", "description": "An innovative teaching-learning pedagogy was developed using customized 3D printed working models for subjects related to Kinematics of Mechanisms and Machine Elements. The pedagogy integrates physical visualization, motion analysis, and experiential learning to improve conceptual understanding of complex mechanical systems. Different mechanism models such as four-bar link