", "score": "48", "planned": "40", "director": "48", "semester": "BBA (2024) Sem IV", "conducted": "38", "course_code": "CSR 2101", "planned_classes": "40", "conducted_classes": "38"}, {"hod": "", "sem": "MBA (2025) Sem I", "code": "MM 5008", "score": "43", "planned": "30", "director": "43", "semester": "MBA (2025) Sem I", "conducted": "24", "course_code": "MM 5008", "planned_classes": "30", "conducted_classes": "24"}, {"hod": "", "sem": "BBA (2023) Sem V", "code": "REI 3010", "score": "50", "planned": "40", "director": "50", "semester": "BBA (2023) Sem V", "conducted": "51", "course_code": "REI 3010", "planned_classes": "40", "conducted_classes": "51"}], "products": [{"hod": "", "used": "Used by companies and certified organic farmers to focus there activities.", "score": "10", "usage": "Used by companies and certified organic farmers to focus there activities.", "details": "Developed a Model on Organic Foods Marketign Strategies on organic foods. Its helpful to increase the product reach and profit and to allocate right amount of resources on riight product.", "director": "5"}], "projects": [{"hod": "", "label": "Guided MBA Semester I students to participate in Techfest, held from 21st to 24th December 2025 at Indian Institute of Technology Bombay. The festival is recognized as Asia’s largest science and technology festival and provided students with exposure to emerging technologies, innovation, and industry trends.  Students were encouraged to attend hands-on workshops in Artificial Intelligence, Robotics, and advanced technologies, along with expert sessions conducted by professionals from leading companies such as Amazon, Google, and BSE India. The event also featured India’s first International Humanoid Summit, showcasing advanced humanoid robots from countries including Austria, China, and India.  Participation in the event helped students gain practical insights into technological advancements, industry applications, innovation ecosystems, and interdisciplinary learning. Students also received an opportunity to earn participation certificates from Indian Institute of Technology Bombay.The following MBA Semester I students participated in Techfest conducted at Indian Institute of Technology Bombay from 21st to 24th December 2025:  Akash Lahane Yuvraj Chavan Gourav Darandale  The students actively participated in workshops, expert sessions, and technology exhibitions related to Artificial Intelligence, Robotics, and emerging technologies. Their participation enhanced their practical exposure to innovation, industry trends, and advanced technological applications.", "score": "5", "director": "5"}, {"label": "Guided MBA-DB student Ms. Shruthi Hinduja in the successful completion of her internship project titled “The Role of Investor Literacy and Market Dynamics in Shaping Investment Behavior Towards Agricultural Category I AIFs: A Study in Salem” conducted at Finnx Software and Pension Tree. The project focused on analysing investor literacy, market dynamics, financial behaviour, and the role of digital fintech platforms in Agricultural Alternative Investment Funds (AIFs).  Provided continuous academic guidance in research design, data collection, analysis, interpretation, and report preparation. The student successfully conducted primary research with investors, analysed financial and behavioural trends, and developed practical recommendations for improving investor awareness and digital financial inclusion. The project enhanced the student’s analytical, research, and professional skills while bridging academic learning with real-world fintech industry practices.", "score": "5", "director": "5"}], "research": [{"hod": "", "name": "Rushikesh Buchkul", "score": "10", "degree": "PG", "thesis": "“A Study of Meta Ads Campaigns for Strategic Digital Growth at Pashium Web Solution.”", "director": "10", "student_name": "Rushikesh Buchkul"}, {"name": "Yash Umbare", "score": "10", "degree": "PG", "thesis": "Study on the Implementa