86864117-60cf-4d0a-b3f3-56fd84930b7d	ganesh.jadhav@dypiu.ac.in	2025-2026	deanfaculties_engineering@dypiu.ac.in	dean	171.5	214.5	386	Dr. Ganesh Jadhav is leading the Mechanical Engineering department very effectively (For SoEMR as well as for DYPIEMR) and uses his excellent industry connections to bring opportunities to the university. He has done outstanding work developing the Dassault Systèmes Centre of Excellence, setting up a Smart Factory in Takshashila for Industry 4.0 learning, and partnering with Atlas Copco for student internships, training, and projects, while also serving as a VC Nominee on the UFM team. To build on these impressive achievements, he needs to work on improving his presentation skills and focus more on securing outside research funding and industry consultancy work. As the Head of Department, it is important for him to excel in these funding and presentation areas so he can truly lead by example for all of his colleagues.	{"acr": [{"dean": "4", "label": "Self-motivation and Proactiveness", "director": "4"}, {"dean": "5", "label": "Punctuality", "director": "5"}, {"dean": "4", "label": "Target based work", "director": "4"}, {"dean": "4", "label": "Effectiveness", "director": "4"}, {"dean": "5", "label": "Obedience", "director": "5"}], "ict": [{"hod": "", "dean": "10", "desc": "Acedemic Website", "quad": "All", "type": "ICT Tool", "score": "10", "title": "Website", "director": "10", "quadrant": "All", "description": "Acedemic Website"}, {"dean": "10", "desc": "Innovative Pedogogy", "quad": "All", "type": "used for Teaching", "score": "10", "title": "AI-Integrated 3D Printed Adaptive Pedagogy for Teaching Kinematics of Mechanism  and Machine Elements", "director": "10", "quadrant": "All", "description": "Innovative Pedogogy"}], "fdps": [{"hod": "", "org": "Autodesk Authorised Partner", "dean": "5", "score": "10", "program": "3D Printed Working Models for Teaching Kinematics of Mechanism and Machine Elements", "director": "5", "duration": "5 Da