ket analysis.", "score": "5", "director": ""}, {"label": "Group Project 2: Business Ethics and CSR Analysis  For this project, two groups from Project 1 will combine to form a larger group of four students. The project focuses on the practical understanding and application of Business Ethics and Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) in real-world industries.", "score": "5"}], "research": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "degree": "", "thesis": "", "director": "", "student_name": ""}], "training": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "nature": "Refresher Course - Pan India", "company": "Refresher Course BY All India Council of Exams", "director": "", "duration": "1 Day"}], "innovRows": [{"score": "2", "method": "Learner-Centered Practical Approach", "details": "Learner-centered and practical teaching approach focused on entrepreneurship, ethics, and CSR."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Active Learning Methods", "details": "Interactive lectures, group discussions, debates, presentations, and project-based learning activities."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Real-Life Case Study Integration", "details": "Regular discussion of real-life case studies, business stories, general stories, startups, industries, and everyday business news."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Visual and Graphic-Based Learning", "details": "PPTs prepared with diagrams, flowcharts, and graphical representations for better understanding and memory retention."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Continuous Learning and Homework Practice", "details": "Preprepartions of the Students"}], "projects2": [{"hod": "", "role": "Consultant", "score": "15", "title": "DYPIU Infrastructure - Interior Projects", "agency": "DYPIU", "amount": "00000", "sanction_date": "01/01/2026", "project_status": "Ongoing"}], "proposals": [{"hod": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "director": "", "duration": ""}], "courseFile": [{"hod": "", "score": "20", "title": "MBA DB SEM II", "course": "ECSR5103 Entrepreneurial Ethics & CSR Program", "details": "1.Available", "director": ""}], "innovScore": "10", "innovDetails": "Learner-Centered Practical Approach, Active Learning Methods, Real-Life Case Study Integration, Visual and Graphic-Based Learning, Continuous Learning and Homework Practice", "externalProjects": [{"hod": "", "role": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "sanction_date": "", "project_status": ""}], "internalProjects": [], "summaryOtherInfo": "Served as the Controller of Examinations and managed all examination-related activities till March 2026. \\nIndependently prepared, edited, and authored a comprehensive Examination Handbook. \\nOrganized Board of Examinations Meeting.\\nManaged Budgets and Finance Approvals, Finance Students data for Audits \\nDeveloped the Remuneration Policy for Examination Duties by benchmarking practices across local universities, public institutions, and premier institutes including IITs. \\nDesigned and implemented the Academic Excellence, Scholarship, Merit, and Medal Policy for Convocation. \\nInvited by various institutes and universities to share knowledge and expertise on examination administration and academic governance. Prepared the Convocation Proceedings and served as a key member of the Convocation Committee, contributing to the successful execution of a grand and well-organized Convocation ceremony.\\nSuccessfully handled and resolved all student grievances related to examinations and academic records in a timely manner. \\nEnsured the issuance and delivery of Marksheets, Provisional Degree Certificates, and Degree Certificates to students ahead of scheduled timelines. \\nLed the implementation and uploading of student academic records on the National Academic Depository (NAD) and Academic Bank of Credits (ABC) portals, facilitating the registration of over 4,800 students and the successful upload of more than 11,000 marksheets and academic awards, ensuring compliance with national digital academic record initiatives.\\nParticipated in all the University activites and strategic formulations.\\nActively involved in the planning, development, and execution of DYPIU construction and interior projects, contributing to space planning, infrastructure development, interior layouts, facility design, and coordination with architects, contractors, and management", "sectionSaveStatus": {"partA": true, "partB": true}, "sectionApplicability": {"society": "notApplicable", "projects": "applicable", "research": "notApplicable"}}, "status": "Pending Director Review", "totals": {"grandTotal": 367.9695, "partATotal": 162.96949999999998, "partBTotal": 205, "effectiveGrandMax": 510, "effectivePartAMax": 165, "effectivePartBMax": 345}, "review_chain": ["director", "dean", "vc"], "academic_year": "2025-2026", "next_reviewer": "director", "workflow_status": "Pending Director Review", "submitter_profile": {"email": "madhura.jagtap@dypiu.ac.in", "school": "SoCM", "full_name": "Dr. Madhura Jagtap", "department": "", "experience": "", "designation": "Professor", "employee_id": "", "qualification": "", "appraisal_role": "faculty", "reportsToRegistrar": false, "teaching_experience": "", "reports_to_registrar": false}, "next_reviewer_role": "director"}	2026-05-29 11:29:33.921571+00	2026-05-30 15:39:56.991312+00
