 academic communication with students."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Conceptual Videos", "details": "Created and shared conceptual YouTube lecture videos for difficult modules including Graph Theory and Algebraic Structures to support student learning and revision before End Semester Examination."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Quiz", "details": "Conducted regular online quizzes through JUNO LMS for continuous assessment, practice, and concept reinforcement across multiple student divisions."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Group Discussion", "details": "Encouraged classroom discussion, interactive questioning, tutorial-based discussions, and active student participation during lectures and problem-solving sessions."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Participatory & Innovative T/L Process", "details": "Implemented participatory and innovative teaching-learning practices through ICT-enabled interactive teaching using pentablet, Xournal, projector systems, tutorial discussions, student interaction, extra academic support sessions, conceptual learning support, and integration of theoretical and practical learning activities."}], "projects2": [{"hod": "", "role": "PI", "score": "15", "title": "Quantum Walk Based Algorithms for Subgraph Isomorphism Detection and Construction", "agency": "DYPIU, Pune", "amount": "230000", "sanction_date": "20/05/2026", "project_status": "In Process"}], "proposals": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "title": "Implementing Quantum Attacks on Kyber: A Post-Quantum Cryptographic Scheme", "agency": "Defence R&D Organisation (DRDO)", "amount": "4024501", "director": "", "duration": "3 years"}, {"score": "10", "title": "Online Quantum Algorithms for Graph-Based Scheduling", "agency": "Anusandhan National Research Foundation (ANRF)", "amount": "8108160", "duration": "3 years"}], "courseFile": [{"hod": "", "score": "20", "title": "B.Tech(CSE), Sem-I, Division A", "course": "CSE1001 (Applied Computational Mathematics)", "details": "1.Available", "director": ""}, {"hod": "", "score": "20", "title": "B.Tech(CSE), Sem-I, Division B", "course": "CSE1001 (Applied Computational Mathematics)", "details": "1.Available", "director": ""}, {"hod": "", "score": "20", "title": "B.Tech(CSE), Sem-II, Division C", "course": "CSE1101 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science)", "details": "1.Available", "director": ""}, {"hod": "", "score": "20", "title": "B.Tech(CSE), Sem-II, Division D", "course": "CSE1101 (Discrete Mathematics for Computer Science)", "details": "1.Available", "director": ""}], "innovScore": "10", "innovDetails": "Blended Learning, Use of Learning Management System (LMS), Conceptual Videos, Quiz, Group Discussion, Participatory & Innovative T/L Process", "externalProjects": [{"hod": "", "role": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "sanction_date": "", "project_status": ""}], "internalProjects": [], "summaryOtherInfo": "(1) Ph.D. Supervisor/Research Guide for doctoral scholars in interdisciplinary research areas.\\n\\n(2) Taught more than 600 students across multiple First Year divisions during Academic Year 2025–26.\\n\\n(3) Lecture delivery, tutorials, assessments, LMS management, course coordination, student support, and academic process monitoring.\\n\\n(4) Participation in Ph.D. candidate interviews, faculty recruitment interviews, and academic evaluation activities.\\n\\n(5) Programme booklet preparation, syllabus development, LaTeX template design, faculty training, and academic documentation coordination.\\n\\n(6) Semester-I teaching commenced after completion of the Student Induction Programme, resulting in a shorter effective teaching period than the standard academic schedule.\\n\\n(7) JUNO ERP/LMS records may occasionally reflect lecture count discrepancies due to timetable mapping, data synchronization, or reporting issues; lesson plans, attendance records, and teaching documents may be referred to for verification.\\n\\n(8) Contribution to university-level academic, admission, examination, ac