uploading course materials, and conducting examination-related activities for SY Chemical Students."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Quiz using Google Forms", "details": "Conducted online quizzes for  SY Chemical students.assessment"}, {"score": "2", "method": "Virtual Lab", "details": "FY Chemical Students gained an understanding of basic fluid flow concepts, Reynolds number, and flow behavior through interactive virtual learning."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Open Course Ware (OCW) assignment", "details": "Conducted an Open Course Ware (OCW) assignment for SY Chemical Engineering students under Numerical Methods tutorials by assigning the Coursera course “Introduction to MATLAB Programming” to enhance programming skills and promote self-learning through online educational resources."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Project Based Learning", "details": "Project-Based Learning activity was conducted for SY Chemical Engineering students through case study-based learning in Chemical Engineering Thermodynamics, where students analyzed real-world topics such as Carnot cycle, refrigeration systems, VLE, heat exchangers, and turbines to connect theoretical concepts with practical engineering applications while enhancing analytical, research, and problem-solving skills"}], "projects2": [{"hod": "", "role": "PI", "score": "15", "title": "Solar Catalyst-Based Water Purification Unit", "agency": "DYPIU", "amount": "10000", "sanction_date": "25/04/2026", "project_status": "Grant Received"}], "proposals": [{"hod": "", "score": "10", "title": "A Bio-Derived Nano Ionic Gel Sensor Utilizing Banana Pseudostem Nanocellulose and A Deep Eutectic Solvent for Soil Nitrate Detection in Real Time", "agency": "DYPIU", "amount": "950000", "director": "", "duration": "1 year"}, {"score": "5", "title": "Green Carbon Quantum Dots for Pesticide Sensing", "agency": "ANRF-ARG-MATRICS", "amount": "500000", "duration": "5 year"}, {"score": "5", "title": "Smart Circular Biorefinery of Waste Flowers and Agricultural Waste for Nano-Fertilizers and Water Purification", "agency": "Cummins  - Venture Center CSR Grant", "amount": "1950000", "duration": "1 year"}], "courseFile": [{"hod": "", "score": "20", "title": "2025-2026(Semester-I)", "course": "ECH2003T /Chemical Engineering Thermodynamics (Theory)", "details": "1.Available", "director": ""}, {"hod": "", "score": "20", "title": "2025-2026(Semester-II)", "course": "ECH2105T /Numerical Methods (Theory)", "details": "1.Available", "director": ""}], "innovScore": "10", "innovDetails": "Juno Learning Management System (LMS), Quiz using Google Forms, Virtual Lab, Open Course Ware (OCW) assignment, Project Based Learning", "externalProjects": [{"hod": "", "role": "PI", "score": "30", "title": "SwissNewater  Pvt Ltd.", "agency": "Swissnewater  Pvt Ltd.", "amount": "1947000", "sanction_date": "23/02/2026", "project_status": "Granted and also doanted equpiment"}], "internalProjects": [], "summaryOtherInfo": "Student-Oriented Work Summary: \\n1. Conducted more than 100% of planned lectures, practical sessions, and tutorials for FY and SY Chemical Engineering students, ensuring effective curriculum delivery and enhanced academic engagement.\\n2. Organized five industrial visits for FY and SY Chemical Engineering students at Lavandar, Khumbha, PCMC, Deepak Fertilizers, and CETP plants (Mumbai/Kurkumbh region) to provide practical industrial exposure.\\n3. Initiated and conducted the first Value Added Course (3O-hour session) for FY and SY Chemical Engineering students under the guidance of Mr. Dudhani Sir, Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Awardee.\\n4. Organized an expert lecture by Dr. Sanjay Kamble, Scientist, NCL Pune, on SDG-14 and plastic waste recycling technologies and processes for FY and SY Chemical Engineering students.\\n5. Organized an expert lecture by Dr. Nalinee Suryawanshi, Director, Swiss NeWater Pvt. Ltd., on Green Hydrogen and emerging technologies in Chemical Engineering.\\n6. Facilitated and coordinated student internships at Swiss NeWater Pvt. Ltd. to provide industrial exposure and practical learning opportunities.\\n7. Initiated and coordinated industrial internship opportunities for SY Chemical Engineering students at Engineering Cluster to strengthen industry-academia interaction.\\n\\nResearch-Oriented Activities:\\n1. Published six research papers in Scopus-indexed journals, contributing to high-quality research dissemination and academic excellence.\\n2. Filed and published one patent based on innovative research work, supporting intellectual property generation and technological advancement.\\n3. Applied for and presented a Seed Funding Project proposal to promote research innovation and interdisciplinary project development.\\n4. Applied for research projects under NCL and ARC Matrics funding schemes to strengthen sponsored research and collaborative opportunities.\\n5. Published three book chapters at national and international levels focusing on emerging research areas and technological advancements.\\n6. Published one book related to sustainable environmental practices and innovative engineering approaches, contributing to academic and research literature.\\n7. Applied as an Editor for a book titled “Emerging Research Areas in Chemical and Environmental Engineering for Sustainable Development” to support scholarly publication and research networking.\\n\\nAdmission-Related Activities:\\n1. Published two newspaper articles in Lokmat and Navbharat highlighting career opportunities and the importance of Chemical Engineering for student awareness and outreach.\\n2. Conducted institute tours for IOPE Lonere students during 2025 and 2026, resulting in positive student interaction and significant admission conversion outcomes.\\n3. Organized career guidance seminars emphasizing the importance of higher education at Camp Education and Mahashant institutions to support FY admissions.\\n4. Conducted offline seminars for diploma students from BATU Lonere, Satara Polytechnic, and Government Polytechnic Thane, and coordinated admission seminars for Jalna Polytechnic students.\\n5. Continuously developed and shared promotional videos, posters, and digital content for admission awareness and department outreach activities.\\n6. Created and managed dedicated WhatsApp groups for students to ensure effective communication, regular follow-ups, and admission-related guidance.\\n7. Maintained continuous interaction with students and parents through calls, counselling, and personalized communication to strengthen admission outreach and engagement activities.\\n\\nAdministrative and Departmental Activities:\\n1. Served as Industrial Visit Coordinator for organizing and managing industrial exposure activities for students to enhance practical learning and industry interaction.\\n2. Acted as Guest Lecture Coordinator for planning and organizing expert sessions by academicians and industry professionals for student development.\\n3. Worked as Feedback Coordinator at Department and School level for effective collection, monitoring, and analysis of academic feedback.\\n4. Served as Examination Coordinator for the First Semester to ensure smooth planning and execution of departmental examination activities.\\n5. Actively contributed as Departmental NAAC Criterion-III Coordinator by supporting research, innovation, and documentation-related activities.\\n6. Worked as Admission Coordinator during the Second Semester and actively participated in student outreach and admission activities.\\n7. Served as Teacher Guardian for FY Chemical Engineering students (Second Batch) for continuous mentoring, academic monitoring, counseling, and tracking students’ progress and overall development.\\n8. Coordinated and facilitated the signing of an MoU with Swiss NeWater Pvt. Ltd. to strengthen industry-academia collaboration, research activities, internships, and student-industry interaction.\\n9. Successfully coordinated the donation and installation of the Swiss NeWater HydroCleaner Machine at DYPIU to support student projects, research activities, innovation development, and future interdisciplinary work in sustainable green technologies and Chemical Engineering applications.\\n10. Actively contributed toward utilizing the donated HydroCleaner system as a research platform for product development, green cleaning technologies, and minimizing harmful chemical utilization through eco-friendly alternatives.\\n\\nSelf-Development and Awards/Appreciation Activities:\\n1. Developed and managed a YouTube channel for students focusing on numerical problem-solving, concept explanations, and fundamental learning support for Chemical Engineering subjects.\\n2. Successfully completed more than 30 Coursera certification courses for continuous professional development and skill enhancement.\\n3. Earned a Coursera Specialization Certificate in Solid Waste Management, enhancing knowledge in environmental sustainability and waste management practices.\\n4. Achieved Elite Grade in the NPTEL course on Chemical Process Safety, demonstrating excellence in specialized technical learning.\\n5. Received Appreciation and Merit Certificates from ISRO/IIRS for successful completion of courses on Remote Sensing and Oceanic Processes with outstanding performance.\\n6. Successfully organized and conducted two Faculty Development Programs (FDPs) at the departmental level to promote academic and research enhancement.\\n7. Participated in more than 10 AICTE FDPs, Refresher Courses, Workshops, and Faculty Development Programs for continuous academic enrichment.\\n8. Attended and presented research papers at two national/international conferences, contributing to research dissemination and scholarly activities.\\n9. Received appreciation on National Science Day for mentoring and guiding students in academic and innovation-related activities.\\n10. Continuously engaged in interdisciplinary learning, digital content development, innovation activities, and research collaborations for professional growth and institutional contribution.\\n11. Developed ICT-enabled teaching-learning resources including digital content, self-created educational videos, and Google Site platforms for student learning support.\\n12. Guided students in innovation activities, Smart India Hackathon projects, internships, and industry-oriented initiatives.\\n13. Established collaborations with industries and external organizations to enhance experiential learning and research opportunities.\\n11. Successfully attended/attending Industrial Training at Engineering Cluster Pvt. Ltd., Swiss NeWater Pvt. Ltd., and completed online Codesoft training under Industrial Internship programs to enhance practical industrial exposure and technical skills.\\n12. Developed an innovative Bacteria Detection Model Kit (Jal Suraksha Kit) through interdisciplinary collaboration involving Chemical Engineering, Microbiology, and 3D Printing laboratories for rapid detection of bacterial contamination in water samples.\\n13. The developed bacteria detection model integrated paper-based analytical devices, smartphone-based monitoring, and colorimetric detection methods for real-time and low-cost water quality analysis.\\n\\n", "sectionSaveStatus": {"partA": true, "partB": true}, "sectionApplicability": {"society": "applicable", "projects": "notApplicable", "research": "notApplicable"}}, "status": "Pending HOD Review", "totals": {"grandTotal": 435.1515, "partATotal": 164.1515, "partBTotal": 271, "effectiveGrandMax": 510, "effectivePartAMax": 165, "effectivePartBMax": 345}, "review_chain": ["hod", "director", "dean", "vc"], "academic_year": "2025-2026", "next_reviewer": "hod", "workflow_status": "Pending HOD Review", "submitter_profile": {"email": "kirti.zare@dypiu.ac.in", "school": "SoEMR", "full_name": "Dr. Kirti Zare", "department": "Chemical Engineering", "experience": "13", "designation": "Assistant Professor,Chemical Engineering", "employee_id": "20251019", "qualification": "Ph.D,MTech (Gold Medalist)", "appraisal_role": "faculty", "reportsToRegistrar": false, "teaching_experience": "13", "reports_to_registrar": false}, "next_reviewer_role": "hod"}	2026-05-20 10:06:03.457812+00	2026-05-26 04:50:16.552291+00
