9d1cf451659c968c_LMS.png"}], "innov-4": [{"url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/faculty-appraisal-uploads/faculty-appraisal/innov-4/70f69d7df178571dcd4528cb93bfed7d00e5fd8ac7a92a2507b4c96d7c49e667_Group_Discussion.png", "name": "Group Discussion.png", "type": "image/png", "publicId": "faculty-appraisal/innov-4/70f69d7df178571dcd4528cb93bfed7d00e5fd8ac7a92a2507b4c96d7c49e667_Group_Discussion.png"}]}, "form": {"acr": [{"label": "Self-motivation and Proactiveness"}, {"label": "Punctuality"}, {"label": "Target based work"}, {"label": "Effectiveness"}, {"label": "Obedience"}], "ict": [{"type": "", "score": "", "title": "", "quadrant": "", "description": ""}], "ipr": [], "fdps": [{"score": "10", "program": "Faculty Development Programme on “Digital Tools and Emerging Technologies for Teaching and Learning”", "duration": "Five-Day", "organization": "School of Skills Development in association with IQAC, D Y Patil International University, Pune (21–25 July 2025)"}, {"_id": 1779960075423.1514, "score": "10", "program": "Faculty Development Programme on “Grants, Funding, and Project Proposal Writing", "duration": "Five-Day", "organization": "School of Skills Development in association with IQAC, DYPIU (07–11 July 2025)"}], "info": {"ay": "2025-2026", "name": "Mr Maan Bardhan Kanth", "qual": "", "desig": "Associate Professor & hod", "school": "SoMCS", "experience": ""}, "books": [{"book": "", "isbn": "", "score": "", "title": "", "coauthor": "", "publisher": "", "first_author": ""}], "confs": [{"type": "Date: 26 July 2025 Represented DYPIU at the Prof. E. V. Chitnis Centenary Conference organized by the National Centre for Science Communicators (NCSC) in collaboration with IISER Pune on the theme “Space Exploration and Innovation for Nation Building.” Interacted with eminent scientists and ISRO dignitaries including Dr. A. S. Kiran Kumar and Dr. Kiran Karnik, contributing towards academic networking and institutional visibility.", "level": "National", "score": 6, "title": "Participation in National-Level Academic Conference", "organization": "IISER Pune"}, {"_id": 1779958496577.9727, "type": "Date: 02 August 2025 Delivered an interactive session for students of Bharati Vidyapeeth, Pune on “Holistic Development of Personality through Indian Knowledge Systems,” promoting value-based education and youth empowerment.", "level": "National", "score": 6, "title": "Expert Session on Holistic Personality Development", "organization": "Bharati Vidyapeeth, Pune"}, {"_id": 1779958636526.726, "type": "Date: 13 September 2025 Coordinated and contributed to the webinar titled “Ancient Wisdom for Modern Skills: Personality Development through Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS)” organized by the School of Skills Development, DYPIU.", "level": "National", "score": 6, "title": "Webinar on Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS)", "organization": "DYPIU"}, {"_id": 1779958731346.7793, "type": "Date: 4th June 2025 Honored to share my thoughts on scientific communication at Nehru Science Centre, Mumbai and the National Centre for Science Communicators.", "level": "National", "score": 6, "title": "My thoughts on scientific communication at Nehru Science Centre", "organization": "Nehru Science Centre, Mumbai"}, {"_id": 1779958834147.5684, "type": "Date: 26 November 2025 Contributed to the successful organization and coordination of Constitution Day celebrations at DYPIU, promoting constitutional values and civic awareness among students.", "level": "National", "score": 6, "title": "Constitution Day Celebration", "organization": "DYPIU"}], "quals": [{"label": "", "score": ""}], "awards": [{"level": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "award_date": ""}], "patents": [], "society": [{"score": "5", "details": "As part of DYPIU’s social outreach initiatives commemorating the birthday of Hon’ble Dr. D. Y. Patil Sir, I actively contributed to community engagement activities in the adopted village of Sathesai, Taluka Mulshi, Pune District. Representing the School of Mass Media & Journalism, I coordinated the donation of dustbins to promote cleanliness, environmental awareness, and sustainable community practices. The initiative involved village-level outreach, stakeholder coordination, and sensitizing students towards social responsibility, sanitation awareness, and community development. Through this contribution, I supported DYPIU’s vision of rural engagement and education-driven social transformation.", "activity": "Unnat Bharat Abhiyan"}, {"_id": 1780038530292.663, "score": "5", "details": "Actively participated in and supported university-led social outreach and wellness initiatives including Yoga Sessions and Blood Donation Drives organized at DYPIU. Contributed towards promoting health awareness, community service, social responsibility, and student participation through coordination, student mobilization, and institutional engagement activities aligned with the university’s commitment to holistic development and social well-being.", "activity": "Social outreach and wellness initiatives including Yoga Sessions and Blood Donation"}], "uniActs": [{"score": 5, "nature": "Played a major leadership and coordination role in organizing “Indus Fiesta 2026,” the annual cultural and academic festival of DYPIU involving large-scale student participation, cultural performances, competitions, and academic activities.", "activity": "Indus Fiesta 2026 : Dates: 22 January – 25 January 2026"}, {"_id": 1779883390110.742, "score": 5, "nature": "Actively involved in planning, stage coordination, protocol management, communication, and smooth execution of the 5th Convocation Ceremony of DYPIU.", "activity": "5th Convocation Ceremony : Date: 05 February 2026"}, {"_id": 1779883497419.2068, "score": 5, "nature": "Contributed to organizing and coordinating the 8th Foundation Day celebrations of DYPIU, reflecting institutional growth and achievements.", "activity": "Foundation Day Celebration : Date: 14 March 2026"}, {"_id": 1779883650757.0127, "score": 5, "nature": "Coordinated and supported the organization of “Samarth Talks,” hosted by DYPIU in partnership with Hyundai and Times Network, focusing on inclusivity and accessibility awareness.", "activity": "Samarth Talks – Inclusivity Initiative : Date: 23 November 2025"}, {"_id": 1779883783667.1487, "score": 5, "nature": "A significant contribution during the academic year was the systematic and structured strengthening of the Student Council framework at DYPIU.  As Director – Student Welfare, I played an instrumental role in initiating, organizing, mentoring, and streamlining student leadership participation through a more structured Student Council mechanism for the first time at the university level. The initiative contributed significantly towards building a more participative, inclusive, and student-centric academic environment at DYPIU.", "activity": "Structured Formation and Strengthening of Student Council"}, {"_id": 1779883929536.2542, "score": 1, "nature": "Actively participated in planning and execution of Alumni Meet 2025, strengthening alumni engagement and institutional networking.", "activity": "Alumni Meet 2025 : Date: 22 November 2025"}, {"_id": 1779884121300.7727, "score": 1, "nature": "Led the Flying Squad Team during end-term examinations, ensuring discipline, transparency, and smooth conduct of examination-related activities.", "activity": "Examination Flying Squad Leadership : Dates: 07 May – 15 May 2026"}, {"_id": 1779884163851.8975, "score": 1, "nature": "Represented DYPIU as a speaker at the Times Education Expo 2026, delivering an expert talk and enhancing institutional outreach and visibility.", "activity": "Representation at Times Education Expo 2026: Date: 17 May 2026"}, {"_id": 1780042143658.1729, "score": 2, "nature": "Actively contributed to the planning, coordination, promotion, and execution of the cultural event “Viksit Bharat Ke Rang, Kala Ke Sang,” which provided a creative platform for DYPIU students to express their vision of a developed India through various forms of art, culture, and creative expression. The event encouraged student participation, artistic innovation, national consciousness, and interdisciplinary engagement aligned with the vision of “Viksit Bharat.”", "activity": "Viksit Bharat Ke Rang, Kala Ke Sang"}], "deptActs": [{"score": 7, "nature": "Actively facilitated and coordinated the Film Appreciation Course conducted in collaboration with Film and Television Institute of India (FTII), Pune, enabling students to gain exposure to cinematic studies and media learning through institutional collaboration.", "activity": "Collaboration Initiative with FTII Pune"}, {"_id": 1779883142510.4875, "score": 7, "nature": "As HoD of the School of Media and Communication Studies, I consistently encouraged and facilitated guest lectures, expert sessions, industry–academia interactions, educational visits, social outreach activities, and industrial tours to provide students with practical exposure and experiential learning opportunities. I also actively contributed towards strengthening the academic and institutional visibility of the School by developing bilingual e-content (Hindi and English) to ensure that the benchmarks, achievements, and innovative initiatives of the School reached a wider student community and promoted inclusive learning.", "activity": "Guest lectures, expert sessions etc."}, {"_id": 1780039243137.5225, "score": 6, "nature": "Actively contributed towards institutional documentation, data compilation, content development, and coordination work related to NAAC quality assurance processes. Played a significant role in preparing and organizing documents for University Criteria–5 and School-Level Criteria–1 for the School of Media and Communication Studies, ensuring systematic presentation of academic, student support, curricular, and institutional quality initiatives in alignment with accreditation and assessment requirements.", "activity": "Documentation work related to NAAC"}], "feedback": [{"score": "7.0", "feedback_1": "70", "feedback_2": "70", "course_code": "JMC 3602 - Environmental Studies and Journalism"}, {"_id": 1780034976486.0461, "score": "5.0", "feedback_1": "50", "feedback_2": "50", "course_code": "JMC 1216 - Indian Knowledge System & Communciation"}], "journals": [{"issn": "", "score": "", "title": "", "journal": "", "indexing": ""}], "lectures": [{"score": 10, "semester": "I", "course_code": "JMC 1110 Indian Folk Culture & Theatre", "planned_classes": "14", "conducted_classes": "11"}, {"_id": 1779880814034.8123, "score": 10, "semester": "II", "course_code": "JMC1217 Indian Political System", "planned_classes": "45", "conducted_classes": "40"}, {"_id": 1779881769056.7556, "score": 10, "semester": "III", "course_code": "JMC 2304 Television Journalism", "planned_classes": "60", "conducted_classes": "60"}, {"_id": 1779881924840.2925, "score": 10, "semester": "III", "course_code": "JMC 2306 Corporate Communication", "planned_classes": "35", "conducted_classes": "35"}, {"_id": 1779882003702.1262, "score": 10, "semester": "II", "course_code": "Indian Knowledge System & Communication(JMC 1216)", "planned_classes": "15", "conducted_classes": "50"}, {"_id": 1779882101508.5217, "score": 10, "semester": "IV", "course_code": "Environmental Studies and Journalism (JMC 3602)", "planned_classes": "45", "conducted_classes": "45"}], "products": [{"score": 20, "usage": "(Link of the Anthem: https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7425640402029789185/)  For the first time in the history of DYPIU, a dedicated university anthem was conceptualized, created, and professionally recorded as a symbol of institutional pride, unity, vision, and cultural identity.  I played a key leadership and creative role in this landmark initiative by contributing as:  Lyricist of the DYPIU Anthem Lead Vocalist/Singer Conceptual Coordinator for Anthem Development  The anthem was musically arranged by Shri Sreyas Deshpande and recorded at the iconic Dawn Studio, Pune — a legendary studio historically associated with Bharat Ratna Lata Mangeshkar.  This initiative stands as a historic contribution towards the cultural and emotional identity of DYPIU.", "details": "Creation of the Historic DYPIU Anthem"}], "projects": [{"label": "Project guided: Guided student projects in Television Journalism", "score": "3"}, {"_id": 1780034050242.701, "label": "Project guided: Guided student projects in Environmental Journalism", "score": "3"}, {"_id": 1780034310297.5957, "label": "Project guided: Guided student projects in Indian Knowledge System and Communication", "score": "4"}], "research": [{"score": "", "degree": "", "thesis": "", "student_name": ""}], "training": [{"score": "", "nature": "", "company": "", "duration": ""}], "innovRows": [{"score": "2", "method": "1.\\tBlended learning", "details": "Combination of classroom teaching with digital resources."}, {"score": "2", "method": "2.\\tVirtual Lab", "details": "Use of newspapers and digital media tools in Television Journalism and Corporate Communication."}, {"score": "2", "method": "3.\\tConceptual videos (list of video shared to students, and class photo of activity)", "details": "Shared conceptual videos related to folk culture, communication campaigns, documentaries, and television reporting."}, {"score": "2", "method": "4.\\tUse of Learning Management System(LMS)", "details": "Learning materials, assignments, presentations, and reference resources shared through JUNO."}, {"score": "2", "method": "8.\\tGroup Discussion (class photo of activity, along with report)", "details": "Organized classroom discussions on environmental issues, corporate case studies, and television journalism practices."}], "projects2": [], "proposals": [{"score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "duration": ""}], "courseFile": [{"score": "18", "title": "B.A. JMC - Sem I", "course": "JMC 1110 Indian Folk Culture & Theatre", "details": "1.Available"}, {"_id": 1780052658742.003