d as a Guest Lectures", "level": "College/ Institute Level", "score": 0, "title": "Creative Art Session", "organization": "D Y Patil Collegeof Engineering,Akurdi Pune"}, {"_id": 1779967936834.0066, "type": "Resource Person -Judging", "level": "College/ Institute Level", "score": 5, "title": "Best Out of WasteCompetition", "organization": "D Y Patil Collegeof Engineering,Akurdi Pune"}, {"_id": 1779967963866.3525, "type": "Resource Person -Judging", "level": "College/ Institute Level", "score": 5, "title": "Studio Design evaluationCompetition For Academic Audit", "organization": "Padmashree Dr DY Patil college ofArchitecture,Akurdi"}, {"_id": 1779968041507.0312, "type": "Resource Person for conduction team of SAAC & Managements students -Judging", "level": "Institute Level", "score": 5, "title": "Management Poster Competition  KalaKRITI 2026", "organization": "Dr. D Y Patil Institute of Management Studies DYPIMS"}, {"_id": 1779985038456.2478, "type": "Conference - Presented Paper", "level": "National", "score": 5, "title": "Dnyadarshan 2026 National Multidislipanary conference", "organization": "Yashwantrao Chavan Maharashtra Open University"}], "quals": [{"_id": 1779794344880.7253, "label": "PhD Pursuing in Visual Arts", "score": "5"}, {"_id": 1779852382039.174, "label": "Packaging Design: Redesign a Product and  Modern Art & Ideas for a Brand from A to Z", "score": "5"}], "awards": [{"_id": 1779794344880.128, "level": "National", "score": 10, "title": "Indian Art Contest", "agency": "MSME Ministry of Micro, Small & Medium Enterprises", "award_date": "30/03/2026"}], "patents": [], "society": [{"_id": 1779794344880.5278, "score": "5", "details": "The School of Applied Arts & Crafts is organising a Face Painting Competition – 2025 under the banner of “Viksit Bharat Ke Rang, Kala Ke Sang.” The competition aims to provide a creative platform where participants can express their imagination, artistic skills, and innovative ideas through face painting. With exciting themes such as Fantasy & Magic, Social Issues, and Festivals, the event encourages participants to explore diverse subjects—ranging from mythical and imaginative visuals to socially relevant messages and cultural celebrations. This event not only promotes artistic expression but also fosters creativity, confidence, and a spirit of community within the institute. It promises to be a colorful and engaging celebration of art and ideas. Summary of Event:  Seva Parv 2025: Colours of a developed India with art The Ministry of Culture, Government of India is celebrating Seva Parv 2025 as a nationwide celebration of service, creativity and cultural pride from 17 September to 2 October 2025. Inspired by Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi's vision of a developed India by 2047, Seva Parv aims to bring together communities, institutions and individuals in a collective movement of service, creativity and cultural pride. As part of the ongoing Seva Parv 2025,( Information by https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleaseIframePage.aspx?PRID=2173828) & On the occasion of Earth Day, the School of Applied Arts and Crafts at D Y Patil International University organized a tree plantation activity on campus to promote environmental awareness and sustainability. As part of this initiative, one team of students actively participated in planting a rubber tree within the university premises. The activity aimed to encourage ecological responsibility, connect students with nature, and highlight the importance of green practices in everyday life. It also reinforced the value of environmental conservation through hands-on experience, making students more conscious of their role in protecting and nurturing the ecosystem for a sustainable future.", "activity": "Face Painting Activity, Sewa Parv 2025 ”Viksit bharat ke rang kala ke sang” & Tree Plantation"}, {"_id": 1779854252700.2124, "score": "5", "details": "Coordinated the university-level Earth Day Awareness Poster Making Competition under the Bharat Environment Program – A Bharat Sustainability Campus Mission 2026. Managed student participation, registrations, communication, and overall event execution while promoting sustainability and environmental awareness through creative poster designs.", "activity": "EARTH DAY POSTER & Reel MAKING COMPETITION 2026"}], "uniActs": [{"_id": 1779794344880.5493, "score": 10, "nature": "social welfare - Viksit Bharat Abhiyan", "activity": "Coordinator of Face Painting Activity"}, {"_id": 1779855692308.674, "score": 10, "nature": "Social Welfare- Bharat Enviornment Programme 2026", "activity": "EARTH DAY POSTER MAKING COMPETITION 2026"}, {"_id": 1779874233731.2593, "score": 0, "nature": "Academic year Activity", "activity": "NAAC Criteria 5.1.2 Univesity level Coordinator"}, {"_id": 1779874288935.1028, "score": 0, "nature": "Short term based- Cutural Program", "activity": "Indust Fiesta Ramp Walk Coordinator"}, {"_id": 1779875795181.7988, "score": 0, "nature": "Short term based Induction Program.", "activity": "Diksharambh Registartion Comitee Member"}, {"_id": 1779884382437.5437, "score": 10, "nature": "Social Welfare- Bharat Enviornment Programme 2026", "activity": "EARTH DAY REEL MAKING COMPETITION"}, {"_id": 1779884453166.066, "score": 0, "nature": "Academic year Activity", "activity": "NAAC University Criteria 8 Coordinator"}], "deptActs": [{"_id": 1779794344880.2385, "score": 5, "nature": "Semester/term based activity", "activity": "Coordinator of Educational Tour -Kerala"}, {"_id": 1779873993034.3657, "score": 0, "nature": "Semester/term based activity", "activity": "Coordinator of Educational Tour -Kerala Artwork Exhibition"}, {"_id": 1779874170019.801, "score": 0, "nature": "Academic Year activity", "activity": "FYBFA Sem I & Sem II Class Mentor"}, {"_id": 1779874192674.0684, "score": 5, "nature": "Academic Year activity", "activity": "NAAC Criteria 5 Coordinator"}, {"_id": 1779874311183.2283, "score": 0, "nature": "Academic Year activity", "activity": "JUNO ERP Academic Admin Module owner for AY 2025-2026"}, {"_id": 1779958153831.2476, "score": 0, "nature": "Short Term Activity", "activity": "Member of AAkruti Annual Art Exhibition"}, {"_id": 1779959421462.6455, "score": 0, "nature": "semester /Term based activity", "activity": "School Feedback Coordinator"}, {"_id": 1779961696393.63, "score": 5, "nature": "Academic Year activity", "activity": "Coordinator of NAAC of SAAC"}, {"_id": 1779962237125.0361, "score": 5, "nature": "Academic Year activity", "activity": "IQAC School Level Coordinator"}], "feedback": [{"_id": 1779794344880.2922, "score": "9.5", "feedback_1": "95.19", "feedback_2": "95.19", "course_code": "Colour Theory & 2-D Design-IAAR-1005"}, {"_id": 1779882423930.0986, "score": "9.4", "feedback_1": "94.4", "feedback_2": "94.4", "course_code": "3D Design, AAR-1006"}, {"_id": 1779882430613.3147, "score": "9.8", "feedback_1": "100", "feedback_2": "95.45", "course_code": "Semiotics - Semantics-II, AAR-1106"}, {"_id": 1779882444322.0122, "score": "9.6", "feedback_1": "100", "feedback_2": "91.38", "course_code": "Fundamentals of Layout, AAR-1107"}], "industry": [{"_id": 1779794344880.5222, "name": "Brand Semiotics and Semantic Analysis through Observational Study of Public Behaviour at Elpro City Square Mall", "score": 0, "details": "rand Semiotics and Semantic Analysis through an Observational Study of Public Behaviour during the Visit to Elpro City Square Mall by FYBFA Students: Industry Connect and Learning through Real-World Research Applied in Design Practice"}, {"_id": 1779853382683.7253, "name": "Kerala Arts & Crafts Village", "score": 5, "details": "The FYBFA students visited the Kerala Arts & Crafts Village (KACV), located in Vellar near Kovalam, Kerala, as part of their industry exposure programme. Spread across 8.5 acres, KACV is a vibrant cultural hub dedicated to preserving and promoting the diverse craft traditions of South Asia. The village hosts over 100 skilled artisans working in dedicated studios, showcasing traditional and contemporary art forms. During the visit, students observed various craft techniques, learned about material processes, and understood the integration of art with marketing and sales strategies. The experience provided valuable real-world insights into artisanship, cultural heritage, and creative entrepreneurship."}, {"_id": 1779875162262.763, "name": "Aditya Chari Illustration workshop", "score": 0, "details": "The illustration workshop conducted by Aditya Chari provided students with valuable industry interaction and practical learning experience. Students explored professional illustration techniques, creative processes, digital art practices, and industry trends. The session helped students understand real-world applications of illustration, portfolio development, storytelling, and career opportunities in the creative and design industry through direct interaction with an industry expert."}], "journals": [{"_id": 1779794344880.94, "issn": "-", "score": 10, "title": "VIT Ruby Jubilee Celebrations (ICADBSL)", "journal": "International Conference on Innovation in Architecture, design, Buisness, Society, language and literature", "indexing": "-"}, {"_id": 1779887110918.2456, "issn": "-", "score": 10, "title": "Dnyandarshan 2026", "journal": "National Multidislipanary conference", "indexing": "-"}], "lectures": [{"_id": 1779794344880.5413, "score": 40, "semester": "FYBFA Semester I", "course_code": "Colour Theory & 2-D Design-IAAR-1005", "planned_classes": "21", "conducted_classes": "21"}, {"_id": 1779796784208.9355, "score": 40, "semester": "FYBFA Semester I", "course_code": "3D Design, AAR-1006", "planned_classes": "6", "conducted_classes": "6"}, {"_id": 1779796788167.2905, "score": 40, "semester": "FYBFA Semester II", "course_code": "Semiotics - Semantics-II, AAR-1106", "planned_classes": "10", "conducted_classes": "10"}, {"_id": 1779796791888.8887, "score": 40, "semester": "FYBFA Semester II", "course_code": "Fundamentals of Layout, AAR-1107", "planned_classes": "15", "conducted_classes": "15"}], "products": [], "projects": [{"_id": 1779794344880.7778, "label": "UG Reaserch Project Guidance", "score": "5"}, {"_id": 1779957828373.0447, "label": "Other than Curriculum -UmbrelaPainting Competition", "score": "5"}, {"_id": 1779957857309.4468, "label": "Other than Curriculum - StudentsParticipated in LanternMakingCompetition", "score": "5"}, {"_id": 1779958392262.2695, "label": "Other than Curriculam - STudents Participoated in YIN Kala Mahostav", "score": "5"}], "research": [{"_id": 1779794344880.1235, "score": "", "degree": "", "thesis": "", "student_name": ""}], "training": [{"_id": 1779794344880.2798, "score": "10", "nature": "Interdisciplinary Collaborative Training", "company": "Dr. D. Y. Patil Institute of Management Studies Students", "duration": "23/03/2026 to 28/03/2026"}], "innovRows": [{"score": "2", "method": "Used LMS -JUNO ERP", "details": "Regular use of the LMS was carried out for effective academic management and student communication. Attendance was updated regularly on JUNO ERP for maintaining accurate student records. Course content, lecture notes, study materials, assignments, and classroom activity details were uploaded for easy student access. Important academic notices, submissions, and subject-related resources were also shared through the platform. The LMS helped in maintaining organized digital records, smooth communication between teachers and students, and continuous learning support throughout AY 2025–2026."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Used Blended learning_Courseera", "details": "The main objective of this blended learning initiative was to encourage students to enhance their knowledge and skills through online learning platforms like Coursera. During AY 2025–2026, every student successfully completed two online courses to gain additional subject knowledge, practical skills, and industry-oriented learning experience. The initiative promoted self-learning, digital learning methods, time management, and continuous skill development beyond classroom teaching. It also helped students improve professional knowledge, creativity, communication, and technical understanding through certified online courses."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Project Based Learning- Earth Day", "details": "Under the Fundamentals of Layout subject, students created Earth Day awareness posters to spread environmental and social awareness. The posters were exhibited on campus, and students presented their concepts before jury members, enhancing creativity, presentation skills, and visual communication understanding."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Field Visit Learning", "details": "FYBFA students visited Elpro City Square Mall for field-based learning to study wayfinding, space design, branding, semiotics, and semantics through real-life observation, market research, and practical learning experiences beyond the classroom."}, {"score": "2", "method": "Educational Tour", "details": "The educational tour to Kerala provided students with learning beyond the classroom through cultural exploration, architectural study, art observation, and experiential learning. The tour enhanced creativity, teamwork, practical knowledge, and real-world understanding"}, {"score": "0", "method": "Creative Character Design and Game Art Activity for First-Year Students", "details": "The event focused on innovative teaching and learning through interactive games conducted by senior student Anshul. The activity created a fun and engaging learning environment, encouraging teamwork, communication, creative thinking, and active participation while promoting peer learning and collaborative interaction among students. Anshul Mesharma is a final-year student whose work in animation is excellent. He is highly skilled in character design, game design, and storytelling for games. His creative ideas and design process are very inspiring for students. Therefore, I planned an activity with first-year students so they could understand character design, game concepts, and creative storytelling more clearly through interactive learning and guidance from a senior student."}, {"score": "0", "method": "Interactive Learning Through Group Discussion and Creative Activities", "details": "The activity encouraged innovative teaching and learning through group discussions, creative thinking, and AI-based techniques. Students explored semiotics, semantics, and wayfinding processes while improving research, teamwork, observation, critical thinking, and presentation skills. AI tools also helped students complete group activities and projects effectively."}], "projects2": [], "proposals": [{"_id": 1779794344880.9631, "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "duration": ""}], "courseFile": [{"_id": 1779794344880.6758, "score": "20", "title": "SAAC FYBFA Semester I", "course": "Colour Theory & 2-D Design-IAAR-1005", "details": "1.Available"}, {"_id": 1779881884515.2085, "score": "20", "title": "SAAC FYBFA Semester I", "course": "3D Design, AAR-1006", "details": "1.Available"}, {"_id": 1779881889642.804, "score": "20", "title": "SAAC FYBFA Semester II", "course": "Semiotics - Semantics-II, AAR-1106", "details": "1.Available"}, {"_id": 1779881894802.2307, "score": "20", "title": "SAAC FYBFA Semester II", "course": "Fundamentals of Layout, AAR-1107", "details": "1.Available"}], "innovScore": "10", "innovDetails": "Used LMS -JUNO ERP, Used Blended learning_Courseera, Project Based Learning- Earth Day, Field Visit Learning, Educational Tour, Creative Character Design and Game Art Activity for First-Year Students, Interactive Learning Through Group Discussion and Creative Activities", "externalProjects": [{"_id": 1779794344880.409, "role": "", "score": "", "title": "", "agency": "", "amount": "", "sanction_date": "", "project_status": ""}], "internalProjects": [{"_id": 1779794344880.4353, "role": "reviewer and Supervisor", "score": "5", "title": "UG Level Reserch Gudance", "agency": "Research Development Cell, DYPIU", "amount": "10000", "sanction_date": "25/04/2026", "project_status": "Approved"}], "summaryOtherInfo": "1. Invited as a resource person and jury member for the event.\\n2. Member of the Art Society of India.\\n3. Departmental/School activities and university-level activities: more than the prescribed marks", "sectionApplicability": {"projects": "applicable", "research": "notApplicable"}}, "status": "Pending Director Review", "totals": {"grandTotal": 309.575125, "partATotal": 174.575125, "partBTotal": 135, "effectiveGrandMax": 520, "effectivePartAMax": 175, "effectivePartBMax": 345}, "review_chain": ["director", "dean", "vc"], "academic_year": "2025-2026", "next_reviewer": "director", "workflow_status": "Pending Director Review", "submitter_profile": {"email": "samata.bendre@dypiu.ac.in", "school": "SoAA", "full_name": "Ms. Samata Sham Bendre", "department": "", "experience": "", "designation": "Assistant Professor", "employee_id": "", "qualification": "", "appraisal_role": "faculty", "reportsToRegistrar": false, "teaching_experience": "", "reports_to_registrar": false}, "next_reviewer_role": "director"}	2026-05-26 12:05:39.90981+00	2026-05-29 13:23:42.943716+00
