496685a6-70c9-477e-902e-d244a455336d	dinesh.kumar@dypiu.ac.in	2025-2026	standard	B3. ICT / E-Content / Pedagogy	\N	2	Noise VIbration and Harshness Simulator	Vibrations Lab Pro is an interactive, web-based NVH simulator that eliminates the need for software installations by operating entirely within the browser. The platform utilizes a custom Runge-Kutta (RK4) physics engine to dynamically solve and visualize complex kinematics for Single-Degree-of-Freedom (SDOF), vehicle suspension, and rotor balancing systems. By allowing users to actively manipulate variables such as mass, stiffness, and damping, the tool provides instant feedback on mechanical responses across various operational regimes. Furthermore, advanced visual analytics translate abstract mathematics into real-time mechanical animations, interactive phase plots, and transmissibility curves using dynamic browser rendering. Ultimately, the simulator bridges theoretical concepts and practical application, empowering students to conduct virtual experiments and export raw CSV data for empirical lab reporting.	Web App	Quadrant III	5	\N	20	\N	\N	2026-05-30 08:32:17.603582+00	2026-05-30 12:24:07.873374+00
